  "id": "COMPOUND:15828 - PROTEIN:6323",
  "verbalization": "Nardosinanol G appears to exert its biological effects through a multi-step pathway that ultimately targets DNA polymerase iota. The evidence suggests that Nardosinanol G acts as a target for CDK2/Cyclin A1, which in turn is targeted by benzopyran or triamcinolone. These compounds, in turn, have a shared target of DNA polymerase iota. This indicates a potential mechanism where Nardosinanol G may influence the activity of CDK2/Cyclin A1, which could then modulate DNA polymerase iota. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Nardosinanol G in regulating DNA polymerase iota through the activation or inhibition of CDK2/Cyclin A1. The evidence supports a dependency on CDK2/Cyclin A1 as a critical mediator in the interaction between Nardosinanol G and DNA polymerase iota, suggesting a complex regulatory network that may be relevant in cellular processes involving DNA replication.",
